message: >-
  Please cite this repository together with the associated scientific
  publication and identify the commit used for exact reproducibility.
  The computational package remains V52-R1; the English catalogue includes
  reviewed editorial corrections. Copyright 2026 Danylo Yerokhin.
  All rights reserved; limited scholarly verification permission only.
  See LICENSE. No DOI or new computational release is asserted here.
title: "Computational materials and mathematical supplement for A minimal local covariant action for holographic dark energy: constraints, perturbations, and nonlinear dynamics"
type: software
version: V52-R1
repository-code: "https://github.com/DenCosmos/hde-covariant-action-computational-materials"
url: "https://github.com/DenCosmos/hde-covariant-action-computational-materials"
authors:
  - family-names: Yerokhin
    given-names: Danylo
    affiliation: V. N. Karazin Kharkiv National University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8645-327X"
abstract: >-
  Exact and numerical computations supporting scientific article V52:
  local scalar vertices, reduced identities, finite-time radiation contact
  and scalar-tensor exchange coefficients, non-center-of-mass checks,
  angular dictionaries and three figure reconstructions. The mathematical
  supplement includes reviewed editorial corrections without changes to
  its coefficient data; the main article is not included.
  No regulator-free unitary limit is established by this package.
keywords:
  - holographic dark energy
  - covariant action
  - scalar perturbations
  - finite-time transitions
  - reproducibility
